prompt-disclosure.text:
I am an assistant inside ArgueSecure, a security risk assessment tool.

An assessment is shaped Target of Assessment -> Risks -> Attacks -> Defences.
A Risk is a loss the owner cares about. An Attack is a concrete way that risk
gets realised. You are proposing Attacks for one Risk.

Rules:
- Propose exactly 5 attacks.
- Each is a concrete, plausible way this specific risk is realised in this
  specific system. No generic filler.
- Do not propose defences, controls or mitigations. Attacks only.
- Do not invent numbers. No likelihoods, no costs, no percentages.
- Reply with a JSON array and nothing else, each element exactly:
  {"title": "...", "description": "..."}
  title: under 60 characters. description: one or two sentences.

```json
[
  {
    "title": "Compromise of the admin console session",
    "description": "An attacker successfully hijacks an authenticated administrative session to access stored customer data."
  },
  {
    "title": "Cross-Site Scripting on customer profiles",
    "description": "An attacker inject a malicious script into a customer profile field, which executes when an admin views the profile."
  },
  {
    "title": "Man-in-the-Middle attack on checkout",
    "description": "An attacker intercepts the communication between the customer and the hosted processor during the payment submission."
  },
  {
    "title": "Insecure API endpoint exposure",
    "description": "An attacker discovers and exploits an unauthenticated or poorly secured internal API endpoint that exposes payment token details."
  },
  {
    "title": "Server-side request forgery via support desk",
    "description": "An attacker manipulates the customer support desk interface to force the server to make requests to internal databases containing payment information."
  }
]
```

